From: j_kro homelab <infra@homelab.local>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: drop broken turbo3_0 FA_COOPMAT2 registration

The retroheim prism fork (176bc4f) registers
CREATE_FA(GGML_TYPE_TURBO3_0, turbo3_0, FA_COOPMAT2, _cm2) inside
#if defined(VK_NV_cooperative_matrix2) && defined(GGML_VULKAN_COOPMAT2_GLSLC_SUPPORT)

but the fork's shader generator never emits a turbo3_0 coopmat2 SPIR-V
variant (the flash_attn MMQ path has no turbo3 code). On a build where
VK_NV_cooperative_matrix2 is exposed by the Vulkan headers, this
instantiation fails to compile with an unresolved
flash_attn_f32_f16_*_cm2_data reference.

Upstream TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant reached the same conclusion:
"cm2 NV-coopmat skipped, fp32-only for turbo3" (a09bafe "vulkan:
restore turbo_wht op + turbo3/4 FA dispatch"). No hardware in this
fleet uses NV cooperative matrix v2 on the Vulkan backend (NVIDIA hosts
run CUDA; AMD Navi 10 has no coopmat2), so the registration is dead
code that breaks the build. Drop it.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -3587,7 +3587,6 @@ static void ggml_vk_create_pipelines(ggml_backend_vk_context * ctx) {
         CREATE_FA(GGML_TYPE_Q8_0, q8_0, FA_COOPMAT2, _cm2)
         CREATE_FA(GGML_TYPE_IQ4_NL, iq4_nl, FA_COOPMAT2, _cm2)
-        CREATE_FA(GGML_TYPE_TURBO3_0, turbo3_0, FA_COOPMAT2, _cm2)
     }
 #endif
 #undef CREATE_FA
